<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary/80 font-medium italic mb-8 border-l-4 border-secondary pl-6">TMJ disorder, also called temporomandibular disorder (TMD), is a group of conditions that affect the jaw joint and the muscles that move it. It usually causes pain, clicking, or limited opening, and in most people it improves with simple self-care, medication, or a bite splint — surgery is needed only in a small minority of cases.</p>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 rounded-xl border border-surface-container-high my-10 not-prose shadow-sm">
